      "claim_id": "L019",
      "reason": "Guideline S005 recommends routine use of gentamicin with benzylpenicillin for empirical treatment of suspected early‑onset infection; AKI is not listed as a contraindication, so withholding gentamicin conflicts with the first‑line recommendation."
    }
  ],
  "critical_omissions": [
    "No alternative antibiotic strategy if gentamicin remains contraindicated (e.g., adding a third‑generation cephalosporin for Gram‑negative coverage) – source S005/S009",
    "No explicit statement to repeat CRP or other labs to guide duration beyond 36 h – source S011"
  ],
  "regimen_incomplete": true,
  "rationale": "The plan follows most NICE recommendations (blood culture before antibiotics, benzylpenicillin dosing, 7‑day duration, monitoring) but deviates by withholding gentamicin without guideline‑supported contraindication, creating a contradiction and leaving the regimen incomplete. Safety is addressed via renal monitoring and nephrology consult, but missing alternative coverage and repeat labs reduce completeness and utility."
}
